WEBVTT

00:04.546 --> 00:06.298
THE FOLLOWING CONTENT CONTAINS DEPICTIONS
OF DOMESTIC ABUSE.

00:06.381 --> 00:07.466
VIEWER DISCRETION IS ADVISED.

00:07.549 --> 00:10.552
[Heeju breathing heavily]

00:12.012 --> 00:13.222
Aren't you tired? Huh?

00:14.014 --> 00:15.265
Why don't you come sit down?

00:15.349 --> 00:16.934
Let's talk a little
and figure this out.

00:17.017 --> 00:20.687
[Heeju breathing heavily]

00:20.771 --> 00:24.024
If you give me the gold bar
and the knife, we can talk.

00:24.107 --> 00:25.651
Ugh, you're being really annoying.

00:27.194 --> 00:28.528
[exhales]

00:28.612 --> 00:31.531
[panicked breathing]

00:31.615 --> 00:33.408
[gold bars clanging]

00:33.492 --> 00:35.244
Closer.

00:37.037 --> 00:38.956
[scraping across floor]

00:39.790 --> 00:40.791
And the knife.

00:45.837 --> 00:47.047
[clatters]

00:49.758 --> 00:52.636
[panicked breathing]

00:52.719 --> 00:55.097
[exhales sharply]

00:56.890 --> 00:58.058
[relieved exhale]

00:58.141 --> 01:01.520
[Woogy] You need to think about this
from an economic perspective, okay?

01:01.603 --> 01:04.398
It really doesn't matter
if it's gold or drugs.

01:04.481 --> 01:07.192
[Woogy] All that matters
is raking in the dough.

01:07.276 --> 01:09.194
Can we turn that item into money or not?

01:09.278 --> 01:12.531
You really think taking the gold bar
to a jewelry shop's a good idea?

01:12.614 --> 01:14.992
[Woogy] A 10-kilogram bar
with a foreign stamp on it?

01:15.075 --> 01:16.451
[exhales]

01:16.535 --> 01:18.453
Okay, just listen.

01:18.537 --> 01:22.040
The jewelry shops, the pawn shops even,
they're all linked to who I work for.

01:22.124 --> 01:24.918
[Woogy] Stuff like gold bars,
that's gonna get around.

01:25.002 --> 01:27.212
You wanna sell a gold bar,
you gotta hand over your phone number,

01:27.296 --> 01:29.131
name, and ID.
So what?

01:29.214 --> 01:31.341
You'll write down,
"Kim Heeju, ID 123?"

01:31.425 --> 01:34.511
You think you can handle all this alone?
You can't.

01:34.595 --> 01:36.430
But I can.
I'm telling you.

01:36.513 --> 01:37.848
My methods are solid.

01:41.059 --> 01:42.436
How do we do it, then?

01:42.519 --> 01:44.730
[exhales sharply]
You a bit more interested now?

01:44.813 --> 01:48.233
Okay, before I lay all this out,
let's make a deal.

01:48.317 --> 01:50.277
-Hey, get back!
-[Woogy] Like partners.

01:50.360 --> 01:52.029
[Heeju] I said get back. Go.

01:52.112 --> 01:53.363
Talk from there.

01:53.447 --> 01:54.740
[exhales sharply]

01:58.076 --> 02:00.746
[Woogy mumbling]

02:02.164 --> 02:04.791
Okay, first, where's the casket?

02:04.875 --> 02:06.668
[Woogy] This can't be everything.

02:07.919 --> 02:09.004
Just tell me where it is.

02:09.087 --> 02:10.839
I need to know exactly
how many bars there are

02:10.922 --> 02:12.007
before I can put a plan together.

02:12.090 --> 02:14.051
Why should I even trust you?

02:15.344 --> 02:16.845
I literally just told you!

02:17.679 --> 02:19.890
If I was gonna rat you out to the boss,
I would have done it already,

02:19.973 --> 02:21.141
and all the guys would be here.

02:23.644 --> 02:26.480
Fine, I wasn't gonna tell you this.
Guess I have to, though.

02:28.148 --> 02:29.358
Look.

02:29.441 --> 02:32.110
[Woogy] That shit hurt.
It still hurts.

02:32.903 --> 02:35.614
They were gonna cut off my ear
if I didn't start talking.

02:35.697 --> 02:37.074
But I held out.

02:37.157 --> 02:40.160
[Woogy] You know why?
'Cause I thought of you.

02:40.243 --> 02:41.828
[exhales]
What the hell?

02:41.912 --> 02:43.622
Why am I such a softie?

02:43.705 --> 02:45.248
[Heeju] Don't make me laugh.

02:45.332 --> 02:48.251
The only reason you showed up here
was to look for the drugs.

02:48.335 --> 02:50.170
If you couldn't find them
you would have threatened me

02:50.253 --> 02:52.214
or done whatever it took
to make me talk.

02:52.297 --> 02:54.216
And once you found them,
you would have killed me.

02:54.299 --> 02:56.343
Oh, really?
Correct me if I'm wrong here,

02:56.426 --> 02:58.762
but you were the one threatening
to shoot me.

03:00.597 --> 03:03.058
Okay, I get it.
Let's move on.

03:03.975 --> 03:05.060
[Woogy] How about this?

03:05.143 --> 03:06.978
Don't tell me where to find the gold.

03:07.062 --> 03:08.480
[Woogy] I won't ask, either.

03:09.147 --> 03:10.148
If you think I'd kill you

03:10.232 --> 03:13.318
and make a run for it after finding out
where the gold is, don't tell me.

03:13.402 --> 03:15.362
[Woogy] If I have no idea,
there's no problem, right?

03:15.445 --> 03:16.988
Instead, how's this?

03:18.115 --> 03:20.325
Every three days,
you give me one gold bar.

03:20.409 --> 03:23.662
[Woogy] Then it'll be up to me
to sell it and bring you the cash.

03:23.745 --> 03:25.580
That means I won't be able
to pull anything funny

03:25.664 --> 03:26.748
until we've sold all the gold.

03:26.832 --> 03:27.916
Make sense?

03:29.918 --> 03:30.919
[Woogy] How many are there?

03:31.002 --> 03:32.504
That I need to know.

03:32.587 --> 03:35.590
[strained breathing]

03:37.759 --> 03:38.760
There's ten.

03:44.599 --> 03:45.684
[Woogy] Ten?

03:45.767 --> 03:50.105
If we sell one for a billion,
times ten is ten billion.

03:50.188 --> 03:51.273
Split it in half.

03:51.356 --> 03:52.524
-[Woogy] Five billion each.
-Split it?

03:52.607 --> 03:53.817
[exhales]

03:54.734 --> 03:56.695
[Heeju] You think it's just you and me?
STYLE
::cue()

03:56.778 --> 03:59.781
It's not our gold.
It belongs to Dokyung.

03:59.865 --> 04:00.991
What? Lee Dokyung?

04:01.074 --> 04:02.617
Nah, he's gonna die soon.

04:02.701 --> 04:05.203
[Woogy] And even if he lives,
he's going to jail anyway.

04:05.287 --> 04:07.080
Wait, why not just cut him out?

04:07.164 --> 04:08.540
What'd you say?

04:09.458 --> 04:10.792
Oh.

04:12.002 --> 04:13.003
What, are you dating?

04:13.920 --> 04:16.131
Am I right?
Is he your boyfriend?

04:16.214 --> 04:18.300
-[groans]
-[Woogy] Eh, doesn't matter.

04:18.383 --> 04:20.051
How is it Lee Dokyung's?

04:20.135 --> 04:21.553
You realize he stole it, right?

04:21.636 --> 04:23.221
So it really belongs to Chairman An.

04:23.972 --> 04:25.056
[Heeju] Okay, then.

04:26.850 --> 04:28.977
[Heeju] So the three of us will split it.

04:29.060 --> 04:30.854
You'll get exactly one-third of the money.

04:30.937 --> 04:32.105
That's your share.

04:33.315 --> 04:34.316
Okay.

04:34.858 --> 04:35.859
Okay!

04:37.319 --> 04:38.320
[exhales sharply]

04:38.403 --> 04:40.530
-So, then.
-[Heeju] What?

04:40.614 --> 04:42.866
-[Woogy] We should fist bump so that...
-Don't come any closer!

04:42.949 --> 04:45.243
Well, we gotta lock in our contract, so...

04:46.620 --> 04:47.746
...fist bump to seal the deal.

04:49.247 --> 04:51.792
First you have to tell me how you plan
on selling the gold bars.

04:52.250 --> 04:53.710
Explain that.
Then I'll decide.

04:53.794 --> 04:55.253
[exhales sharply]
Are you serious?

04:56.296 --> 04:57.297
What the...

04:58.423 --> 05:00.509
[Woogy] Fine. Listen carefully.

05:00.592 --> 05:04.930
[Woogy] Gold is traded in hundreds
of forms in shops across the country.

05:05.013 --> 05:07.682
Gold rings, gold pigs, random stuff.

05:07.766 --> 05:09.768
And the gold bar.

05:09.851 --> 05:14.356
The one-kilogram bars are the easiest ones
for us to trade.

05:14.439 --> 05:18.318
Everything changes depending on
the weight, purity,

05:18.401 --> 05:19.778
and where it was manufactured.

05:19.861 --> 05:23.782
So first we gotta break these down
into one-kilo bars

05:23.865 --> 05:25.450
-and recast them.
-[Heeju] Who can do that?

05:26.368 --> 05:28.370
-[Heeju] You?
-[Woogy] No.

05:28.453 --> 05:30.622
We'll obviously need a goldsmith for that.

05:30.705 --> 05:32.624
Then there's the actual sale.

05:32.707 --> 05:35.168
Selling a 10-kilo bar would be hard,

05:35.252 --> 05:36.837
but small ones, well,

05:36.920 --> 05:39.005
jewelry stores have
no problem buying those.

05:39.923 --> 05:43.134
All of Gwangwon-do has ties to our company
so that won't work.

05:43.218 --> 05:45.303
I'll have to go to jewelry stores
in other areas

05:45.387 --> 05:47.639
and sell only one bar per store.

05:47.722 --> 05:50.016
The whole process of recasting
a bar to selling it

05:50.100 --> 05:53.311
shouldn't take any more than, say,
three days.

05:53.395 --> 05:55.939
So selling them all should take a month.

05:56.022 --> 05:57.816
And to avoid being tracked by the cops,

05:57.899 --> 06:00.277
we gotta make all
of our transactions in cash.

06:00.360 --> 06:03.530
Not to mention, we'll need fake IDs,
burner phones, and burner bank accounts.

06:03.613 --> 06:07.033
But I'll be taking care of all that,
so don't you worry about a thing.

06:07.117 --> 06:08.785
SAMJIN GOLD EXCHANGE

06:11.830 --> 06:15.125
And Heeju,
let's make one thing clear.

06:16.918 --> 06:19.212
[Woogy] Until we've sold all ten gold bars
and split the cash,

06:19.296 --> 06:20.714
we trust each other.

06:22.757 --> 06:26.052
[Woogy] Never, seriously never...

06:27.012 --> 06:30.390
Ever, ever, ever,
never betray each other.

06:30.473 --> 06:32.893
[Woogy] Do you promise?
If not, we're both dead.

06:33.852 --> 06:36.730
You'll be discovered in that mining town
hanging from your neck.

06:36.813 --> 06:38.607
And as for me,
I'm screwing the company over, too,

06:38.690 --> 06:42.319
so I'll get something chopped off
and become a cripple.

06:45.030 --> 06:46.323
You know what I'm saying?

06:47.657 --> 06:48.658
[exhales]

06:50.577 --> 06:52.329
You're the one I'm worried about.

06:52.412 --> 06:53.747
[exhales]

06:57.083 --> 06:58.126
[exhales sharply]

06:58.209 --> 06:59.711
[Woogy] Okay.

07:00.587 --> 07:01.838
[Woogy grunts]

07:03.548 --> 07:04.966
Do this to sign the contract.

07:05.050 --> 07:07.218
Hmm? Deal?

07:13.266 --> 07:15.602
You gotta say "deal" when you do it.
That's how it works.

07:15.685 --> 07:17.020
Deal.

07:17.103 --> 07:18.146
[scoffs]

07:21.858 --> 07:22.859
Deal.

07:24.027 --> 07:25.278
[exhales sharply]

07:28.031 --> 07:29.032
[exhales]

07:29.115 --> 07:30.116
[Woogy] Finally.

07:32.827 --> 07:35.830
[♪ tense music]
STYLE
::cue()

07:53.473 --> 07:56.476
[♪ tense music continues]

08:13.743 --> 08:16.454
[crows cawing]

08:16.538 --> 08:21.251
EPISODE 3
PARTNERSHIP

08:21.334 --> 08:22.335
[Jinman] Yeah.

08:25.880 --> 08:27.340
[clears throat]

08:27.424 --> 08:29.884
[Jinman groans]
Goodness.

08:29.968 --> 08:31.344
[Jinman clears throat]

08:31.428 --> 08:33.513
[metal creaking]

08:36.266 --> 08:38.893
[chains rattling]

08:39.811 --> 08:41.896
[Jinman] Careful.
Ugh, shit.

08:41.980 --> 08:43.356
[camera shutter clicks]

08:44.566 --> 08:46.067
SEOYOON, YERIN, I'M SORRY FOR GOING FIRST.
TO EVERYONE WHO WAS HARMED BECAUSE OF ME,

08:46.151 --> 08:47.610
I AM SORRY. THIS IS THE LAST CHOICE
I CAN MAKE. I'M SORRY. I'M SO SORRY.

08:49.237 --> 08:50.238
Hold up. Stop.

08:57.245 --> 08:58.413
[camera shutter clicks]

09:00.707 --> 09:02.876
[indistinct chatter]

09:04.961 --> 09:06.087
Go, yeah.

09:08.173 --> 09:09.257
Should I send him to forensics?

09:09.340 --> 09:10.717
Nah, just the morgue is fine.

09:10.800 --> 09:11.885
-Yes, sir.
-Yeah.

09:11.968 --> 09:13.303
-[Male Police Officer] The morgue.
-[groans]

09:13.386 --> 09:15.138
[clicks tongue, clears throat]

09:15.221 --> 09:18.224
[cell phone vibrating]

09:19.559 --> 09:21.311
-Take him to the morgue.
-[Male Police Officer] Understood.

09:21.394 --> 09:25.273
[cell phone vibrating]

09:25.356 --> 09:26.399
[exhales]

09:28.693 --> 09:30.779
Ah, I did it. Yeah.

09:30.862 --> 09:32.989
I took care of it like you asked.

09:33.073 --> 09:34.783
Who wrote that note, though?

09:35.992 --> 09:37.786
Looked like President Go's handwriting.

09:39.788 --> 09:41.831
You gotta stop with all
these useless theatrics.

09:41.915 --> 09:44.334
It's a waste.
Just keep your guys in line.

09:45.460 --> 09:46.544
[Hocheol] Thanks for your work.

09:47.712 --> 09:49.297
See you soon, Detective.

09:49.380 --> 09:50.423
Sounds good.

09:51.299 --> 09:52.300
[cell phone beeps]

09:52.383 --> 09:55.178
GANGWON SAEBAEK HOSPITAL

09:55.261 --> 09:57.847
[machine rumbling]

10:06.147 --> 10:07.482
[Sunok exhales]

10:07.565 --> 10:09.359
What the hell have we been doing all day?

10:10.026 --> 10:11.945
We left the shop unattended.

10:12.028 --> 10:13.321
[Female Nurse] Ms. Yeo Sunok.

10:13.404 --> 10:15.240
Here. Come on.

10:22.372 --> 10:23.581
[Male Doctor grunts]

10:24.499 --> 10:25.792
[Male Doctor] Hello.

10:25.875 --> 10:27.335
Could the patient wait outside?

10:27.418 --> 10:29.170
I'd like to speak with the guardian first.

10:29.254 --> 10:32.006
-Uh...
-You can just talk.

10:32.090 --> 10:33.591
I already know anyway.

10:34.592 --> 10:35.927
[all exhaling sharply]

10:37.345 --> 10:41.558
You were diagnosed here a year ago,
but you never went to another hospital?

10:41.641 --> 10:43.351
-No.
-[Male Doctor groans]

10:43.434 --> 10:45.270
[Male Doctor] We should
have started treatment then.

10:45.353 --> 10:46.813
We're a little late now.

10:47.814 --> 10:48.940
If you look here,

10:49.023 --> 10:52.235
you'll see that the tumor cells
have metastasized to the lungs.

10:52.318 --> 10:53.528
[Sunok grunts]

10:53.611 --> 10:56.614
[Male Doctor] Were you feeling okay?
I imagine the pain would be quite severe.

10:57.866 --> 11:00.076
Could surgery be an option?

11:00.160 --> 11:01.911
She should get hospitalized first.

11:02.662 --> 11:04.122
I recommend an examination,

11:04.205 --> 11:06.666
then beginning chemotherapy
to slow down the metastasis.

11:06.749 --> 11:08.835
[Male Doctor] As for surgery,

11:08.918 --> 11:11.212
let's see how things progress
and then decide.

11:11.796 --> 11:14.465
-'Kay.
-So my cancer's in the final stage.

11:14.549 --> 11:16.259
Wouldn't surgery be useless?

11:16.342 --> 11:19.053
[Male Doctor exhales sharply]
Well, when it comes to stages,

11:19.137 --> 11:20.221
you could say that, however...

11:20.305 --> 11:21.431
How much longer do I have?

11:21.514 --> 11:24.642
A specific time frame
is hard to determine at this point.

11:24.726 --> 11:26.686
If I get treatment, I can live...

11:27.270 --> 11:28.605
...how much longer?
Into my 80s?

11:28.688 --> 11:31.566
-Auntie.
-[Sunok] I knew it'd be like this.

11:31.649 --> 11:33.151
They wanna fill me with drugs...

11:33.818 --> 11:36.196
...and poke me with needles even though
I'm dying anyway.

11:36.279 --> 11:39.574
That's how hospitals make money, isn't it?
Hey, we're leaving.

11:39.657 --> 11:40.909
-Auntie!
-Get up. I'm done with all this.

11:40.992 --> 11:42.869
Auntie, please wait! Seriously!

11:44.120 --> 11:45.121
[exhales sharply]
STYLE
::cue()

11:46.664 --> 11:48.791
-Auntie.
-Just forget it.

11:48.875 --> 11:51.127
Oh, come on, please!

11:51.211 --> 11:52.629
I said forget it!

11:52.712 --> 11:54.464
These guys are all crooks.

11:54.547 --> 11:56.382
They don't deserve our hard-earned money.

11:56.466 --> 11:59.010
If this is really about the money,
don't worry.

11:59.093 --> 12:00.803
-I have it.
-[Sunok] Where? Show me.

12:00.887 --> 12:02.388
I wanna see some before I die.

12:02.472 --> 12:05.141
[groaning]

12:06.726 --> 12:08.478
Aren't you in a lot of pain right now?

12:09.187 --> 12:11.689
This is about more than
just you living longer.

12:11.773 --> 12:13.775
Come on.
You're not dead yet.

12:13.858 --> 12:16.945
At least let them give you something
to ease the pain while you're still alive.

12:18.363 --> 12:20.156
Since when did you worry
about me like this?

12:21.616 --> 12:23.159
You were the one who ran off
to live your own life.

12:25.453 --> 12:28.998
And now that I'm dying,
you suddenly have a sense of duty?

12:29.082 --> 12:31.626
You're the one who needs to have
a sense of duty.

12:31.709 --> 12:35.213
What kind of mother wants to just die
and leave their kid by themself?

12:37.382 --> 12:38.675
Am I your mother?

12:39.550 --> 12:40.551
Well, aren't you?

12:41.386 --> 12:43.554
You gave birth to me.

12:48.351 --> 12:49.978
[Sunok] You think I had you
'cause I wanted to?

12:51.771 --> 12:52.855
[exhales sharply]

12:56.150 --> 12:57.277
[sighs]

13:04.242 --> 13:07.245
[bus engine rumbling]

13:40.570 --> 13:43.573
[engine revving]

13:43.656 --> 13:49.579
WELCOME TO GOLD LAND
THE CITY OF DREAMS AND HOPES

13:50.496 --> 13:53.124
[Jinman groans]

13:54.250 --> 13:56.794
[humming]

13:56.878 --> 13:57.879
Hey.

14:01.132 --> 14:03.342
Yeah...

14:04.010 --> 14:07.180
[Jinman] What's this?
I expected a nice spread.

14:07.263 --> 14:10.141
[Jinman] Ah, come on.
Guess not.

14:10.224 --> 14:11.976
So disappointing.

14:13.352 --> 14:16.230
[Jinman] Anyway, I guess the chairman
isn't back from overseas.

14:17.273 --> 14:18.483
I must say, you're looking great.

14:19.817 --> 14:21.611
[Jinman] It must be fun playing
the chairman.

14:21.694 --> 14:23.404
[Hocheol] Lee Dokyung's cell phone.

14:23.488 --> 14:25.114
[Hocheol] Same guy you were tracking
a few days ago.

14:25.198 --> 14:27.492
-Does that mean he's dead?
-[Hocheol] No, he's in the hospital.

14:27.575 --> 14:29.577
But now the cops are on his tail.

14:29.660 --> 14:31.287
Hence our little meeting here.

14:31.370 --> 14:34.207
Not much I can do.
Not if the police are on him. No way.

14:34.290 --> 14:36.042
I'm not asking you to do anything
to Lee Dokyung.

14:37.668 --> 14:40.963
Just take this phone
and use it to find a person.

14:43.216 --> 14:45.051
No way he's working alone.

14:46.219 --> 14:47.220
He's got an accomplice.

14:48.179 --> 14:51.891
A stupid fuck who took off with
the van carrying all of our stuff.

14:51.974 --> 14:53.017
[inhales]

14:53.976 --> 14:55.436
Ah, the casket.

14:56.312 --> 14:57.814
Ah, that must be a headache.

14:58.815 --> 15:02.527
Just dig through his calls and texts
and see what you can find.

15:02.610 --> 15:05.571
You can't expect me to do all that.
Come on.

15:05.655 --> 15:07.990
Searching through
a phone like that's illegal.

15:08.074 --> 15:09.534
And it takes too much time.

15:10.743 --> 15:13.037
Too much money, too.

15:13.121 --> 15:14.622
I'll give you the money,
so don't worry.

15:14.705 --> 15:15.873
[Jinman] Oh, yeah.

15:15.957 --> 15:17.333
Let me think about it, okay?

15:17.416 --> 15:18.417
[Hocheol exhales sharply]

15:18.501 --> 15:19.710
There's no time for thinking.

15:20.878 --> 15:22.755
I gotta do this before
the chairman returns.

15:22.839 --> 15:24.590
And when is that?

15:25.633 --> 15:27.677
At the end of the month.

15:27.760 --> 15:29.095
I am curious, though.

15:29.804 --> 15:30.847
What's in the casket?

15:31.472 --> 15:32.557
Do you know?

15:32.640 --> 15:35.560
[Jinman] Drugs? Meth?

15:36.394 --> 15:37.728
Organs?

15:37.812 --> 15:40.940
Ah, you gangster assholes keep getting
into organ trafficking these days.

15:41.023 --> 15:42.024
You just can't help yourselves.

15:42.108 --> 15:43.818
[Hocheol] Why the fuck do you need
to know everything?

15:45.069 --> 15:46.445
Just do what you usually do.

15:47.405 --> 15:49.157
Do what I'm telling you.

15:53.286 --> 15:54.871
Ah, hold on.

15:57.832 --> 16:01.878
Do I look like the kind of guy who
just does whatever you tell him to?

16:04.255 --> 16:05.798
Of course I'm that guy.

16:06.716 --> 16:07.717
[Jinman] Right.

16:07.800 --> 16:09.385
[Hocheol scoffs]

16:09.468 --> 16:11.470
[Jinman] Fine, fine, I'll do it.

16:11.554 --> 16:12.555
Huh?

16:15.349 --> 16:17.852
Ah, dammit.
STYLE
::cue()

16:17.935 --> 16:20.855
GANGWON CENTRAL POLICE AGENCY

16:20.938 --> 16:22.648
[distant sirens blaring]

16:26.569 --> 16:29.238
[car door opens]
Oh. Oh, there you are.

16:29.322 --> 16:30.781
[grunting]

16:30.865 --> 16:32.658
-Here.
-Yeah.

16:34.410 --> 16:35.870
[coughs]

16:38.998 --> 16:40.416
Read it, then shred it.

16:40.499 --> 16:42.960
You leave that lying around,
you'll get audited or somethin'.

16:43.044 --> 16:47.006
Oh. You think you're all that just 'cause
you're stationed at headquarters now?

16:48.716 --> 16:50.009
I'm your senior.

16:51.093 --> 16:52.053
ON-SITE INVESTIGATION REPORT

16:52.136 --> 16:53.137
[Detective Kang] It's a burner car.

16:53.221 --> 16:54.555
The plate number is fake, too.

16:54.639 --> 16:56.015
Dash cam?

16:56.098 --> 16:57.099
Nothin'.

16:57.183 --> 16:58.893
No surveillance cams in the area, either.

16:58.976 --> 17:00.353
So we don't know who the driver is.

17:01.729 --> 17:02.730
Why?

17:03.731 --> 17:04.982
The casket?

17:05.066 --> 17:06.484
Those Geumseong guys didn't take it?

17:06.567 --> 17:08.194
I don't think so.

17:08.277 --> 17:09.528
What does that mean?

17:09.612 --> 17:10.863
They either took it or they didn't.

17:10.947 --> 17:12.823
So why do you need all this?

17:13.991 --> 17:16.077
To keep Lee Dokyung quiet
in case he wants to talk?

17:16.786 --> 17:19.497
-Maybe.
-Uh, wait a minute.

17:20.081 --> 17:22.083
I'm not gonna be party to a murder.

17:22.166 --> 17:23.918
If that's the plan then I'm done.

17:24.001 --> 17:25.544
This is the last time I'm helping.

17:25.628 --> 17:27.880
You can tell Park
I'm not doing this anymore.

17:27.964 --> 17:31.092
And doing this will pay off my debts.

17:31.175 --> 17:33.678
[distant sirens wailing]

17:33.761 --> 17:34.762
Hey.

17:36.097 --> 17:37.723
How big of a hole are you in?

17:37.807 --> 17:39.684
100 million won?

17:40.643 --> 17:43.980
Oh, man, you really poured it down
the drain, didn't you?

17:44.063 --> 17:45.064
[groans]

17:45.898 --> 17:48.776
What do you like to play?
Baccarat?

17:49.694 --> 17:51.904
Ah, it won't be easy
to climb outta that hole.

17:54.657 --> 17:55.700
What about you?

17:56.325 --> 17:58.119
How much debt did you end up with?

17:58.202 --> 17:59.745
10 billion won?

18:00.913 --> 18:03.040
That's why you're still in this.
Ever since you were a patrol cop,

18:03.124 --> 18:05.001
you've been cleaning up shit
that Geumseong leaves for you, right?

18:05.084 --> 18:07.044
I paid them all back already.

18:07.670 --> 18:09.171
[Detective Kang] Oh, is that so?

18:09.255 --> 18:12.049
Well, if you're debt free then cleaning
up shit must be in your nature.

18:12.133 --> 18:13.593
[pages flip]

18:15.094 --> 18:16.929
-[Detective Kang exhales]
-You know what?

18:19.765 --> 18:21.517
You're a little shit.

18:21.601 --> 18:23.102
Better watch your mouth.

18:25.354 --> 18:26.689
Actually...

18:28.691 --> 18:29.859
My wife is very sick.

18:32.820 --> 18:34.071
That so?

18:35.906 --> 18:37.074
[Detective Kang exhales]

18:37.158 --> 18:39.744
I'm going.
I don't want to see you again.

18:39.827 --> 18:41.746
Hey, hey, hey.

18:41.829 --> 18:45.249
At least tell me what's
in there before you go. Yeah?

18:45.333 --> 18:46.709
Whatever the hell it is,

18:46.792 --> 18:49.211
it's making the guys
at headquarters crazy.

18:49.295 --> 18:51.130
And yet Narcotics are being awfully quiet.

18:51.213 --> 18:52.673
So I guess it's not drugs.

18:52.757 --> 18:54.717
Park didn't tell you anything?

18:57.136 --> 18:58.387
Maybe he doesn't know.

18:58.471 --> 19:00.473
Then what is it?
Come on, just tell me.

19:01.140 --> 19:02.308
-Huh?
-[exhales]

19:03.643 --> 19:07.021
We got the information from Interpol
and it's still under review.

19:07.104 --> 19:08.481
You cannot leak this.

19:08.564 --> 19:10.274
All right, all right, prick.

19:14.236 --> 19:15.321
Gold bars.

19:18.115 --> 19:19.158
Gold bars?

19:21.410 --> 19:23.663
[Detective Kang] There's a Cambodian
trading company funded

19:23.746 --> 19:25.456
by the drug cartel, Krom thom.

19:25.539 --> 19:29.251
The word is that the chairman buried
a massive slush fund.

19:29.335 --> 19:31.504
Under the ground.
Like, actually buried it.

19:32.880 --> 19:34.715
-[scoffs]
-Not cash, but gold bars.

19:34.799 --> 19:36.467
Ten tons worth.

19:36.550 --> 19:39.387
[Detective Kang] Somehow all
this information got leaked.

19:39.470 --> 19:40.971
And the government launched
a massive search

19:41.055 --> 19:42.807
and seizure for tax evasion.

19:42.890 --> 19:46.435
So all those gold bars,
they quickly moved them overseas.

19:46.519 --> 19:48.813
One ton of 10-kilogram gold bars
per shipment,

19:48.896 --> 19:51.148
disguised as caskets. However...

19:52.191 --> 19:53.776
...one was found
at the airport in Hong Kong.

19:54.360 --> 19:56.153
And apparently another one is in Korea.

19:56.237 --> 19:58.155
And that's the casket, huh?

19:58.239 --> 20:00.282
-The one with a ton of gold?
-Yeah, probably.

20:02.326 --> 20:03.411
[Detective Kang] And besides,

20:03.494 --> 20:06.330
that's the only casket that's come in
from Cambodia recently.

20:16.173 --> 20:19.176
[crickets chirping]

20:33.899 --> 20:34.942
[tires squeak]

20:36.235 --> 20:37.695
[gears shift]

20:41.574 --> 20:45.035
SEONGOGAE REST AREA
STYLE
::cue()

20:58.841 --> 21:01.677
-Is anybody here?
-[Female Store Owner] Hi, there.

21:01.761 --> 21:03.846
-Yes, hello.
-[Female Store Owner] Ah, yes.

21:03.929 --> 21:06.932
Excuse me,
but the surveillance camera outside,

21:07.016 --> 21:08.184
did you install it?

21:08.934 --> 21:10.394
[Female Store Owner] Yes.

21:10.478 --> 21:12.104
Well, I'm with the police. Here.

21:12.188 --> 21:13.522
I'm Detective Kim Jinman.

21:13.606 --> 21:16.859
I reported the installation of that camera
to the police already.

21:16.942 --> 21:18.152
Might there be an issue?

21:18.235 --> 21:20.029
Oh, no, no.
It's nothing like that.

21:20.112 --> 21:22.531
There was a traffic accident out front
a few days ago.

21:22.615 --> 21:24.575
-I just want to check something out. Yeah.
-[Female Store Owner] I see.

21:25.826 --> 21:27.244
[mouse clicking]

21:27.328 --> 21:30.331
[computer hard drive clicking]

21:33.209 --> 21:34.251
[mouse clicks]

21:35.169 --> 21:36.420
GANGWON CENTRAL POLICE AGENCY
TRAFFIC INFORMATION CENTER

21:36.504 --> 21:37.797
-One moment. I'll take a look.
-[Jinman] Yeah.

21:37.880 --> 21:39.757
[clicking]
[Female Police Officer] Okay.

21:39.840 --> 21:42.968
12:29 A.M.
Jingogae Intersection.

21:43.052 --> 21:46.764
And at 12:57 A.M.,
21 Jinbu Street.

21:46.847 --> 21:50.851
Next, at 1:32 A.M.
National Route 59.

21:50.935 --> 21:52.353
[Female Police Officer]
And at 1:55 A.M.,

21:52.436 --> 21:54.021
crossing Jeongsan Bridge.

21:54.939 --> 21:56.023
Jeongsan?

21:57.107 --> 21:58.317
[Female Police Officer] Yes.

21:59.401 --> 22:00.861
GEUMSEONG TOURIST HOTEL

22:00.945 --> 22:06.617
[All] ♪ I'm begging you please
Don't cling to me anymore ♪

22:06.700 --> 22:08.285
[Jinman] ♪ Don't come looking for me ♪

22:08.369 --> 22:09.620
Stop it.

22:09.703 --> 22:12.498
Ah, honey, it's fine.

22:12.581 --> 22:14.875
Wow, what's up with your hands?

22:14.959 --> 22:16.418
They're so pretty for a man.

22:16.502 --> 22:18.003
Because they're woman's hands.

22:18.087 --> 22:19.922
That means it's fine if I touch you,
right?

22:20.005 --> 22:21.465
[Jinman] Just kidding!

22:21.549 --> 22:25.386
♪ A heartless girl
when I'm already breaking inside ♪

22:25.469 --> 22:26.929
Park Hocheol's here!

22:27.012 --> 22:28.848
♪ So now just for a while... ♪

22:28.931 --> 22:29.849
CANCEL

22:29.932 --> 22:30.933
-[Jinman] Hey.
-What?

22:31.016 --> 22:32.560
-I finally found my love today!
-Get him outta here.

22:32.643 --> 22:34.270
-It's no fair!
-I know, I know.

22:34.353 --> 22:35.604
-[Jinman] Oh, honey.
-[laughing]

22:35.688 --> 22:38.315
[Jinman] You know, right?
My love?

22:38.399 --> 22:40.818
Honey, I have to be really honest
with you.

22:40.901 --> 22:42.486
Jeongah.

22:42.570 --> 22:43.779
Sorry!

22:44.655 --> 22:46.240
Oh, look.
Park has arrived.

22:46.323 --> 22:48.659
[Jinman] Right when we're getting
this party started.

22:48.742 --> 22:49.952
[door closes]

22:50.035 --> 22:52.204
I'm taking two of those girls out with me.

22:52.288 --> 22:54.999
-Have you found anything?
-[Jinman] Of course I did!

22:55.082 --> 22:56.584
Wait, what did I...

22:57.501 --> 22:59.003
You talkin' about the van?

22:59.670 --> 23:01.630
Yeah, I've been looking around for it.

23:01.714 --> 23:04.091
I combed through the surveillance cameras
in Gangwon-do.

23:04.174 --> 23:05.509
I checked every single one.

23:05.593 --> 23:07.136
Quit rambling and just spit it out.

23:08.721 --> 23:09.722
Hey.

23:09.805 --> 23:11.891
[Jinman] I'm taking two of them today.

23:12.433 --> 23:14.018
-Yes, sir.
-[Jinman] Yeah? You got it?

23:14.101 --> 23:15.144
-[Jinman] Huh?
-[Hocheol] Hey.

23:15.227 --> 23:16.729
-Move it.
-[Jinman] Yeah.

23:16.812 --> 23:18.606
Yeah, go get-
what are you doing?

23:18.689 --> 23:21.025
[Jinman] Go. Get them ready.
Good.

23:22.359 --> 23:23.777
Ah.

23:23.861 --> 23:25.446
[Jinman] What was I saying?

23:26.614 --> 23:28.073
[Jinman] Oh, right. The van.

23:28.991 --> 23:33.287
Was last seen here in Jeongsan.
Where we are.

23:33.370 --> 23:36.123
[Jinman] It was caught
on surveillance cameras.

23:36.206 --> 23:39.460
It shows up at the entrance
to Jeongsan Bridge.

23:39.543 --> 23:40.961
[Jinman] Then no trace of it anywhere.

23:41.045 --> 23:42.421
And two days later,

23:42.504 --> 23:45.633
they dump the van
at the abandoned warehouse,

23:45.716 --> 23:47.176
but it was empty.

23:47.927 --> 23:50.804
[Jinman] So where did they hide
the casket? Huh?

23:50.888 --> 23:52.306
[Hocheol exhales]

23:52.389 --> 23:54.141
[clacks on table]
Right here.

23:54.224 --> 23:55.768
Jeongsan.

23:55.851 --> 23:57.978
They hid it here.

23:58.062 --> 24:00.648
So who was it, then?
The prick who was driving it?

24:00.731 --> 24:02.524
Oh, I don't really know about that.

24:02.608 --> 24:06.487
But either way, I've really
helped you narrow it down.

24:06.570 --> 24:09.698
Just find out who was in Jeongsan that day
and catch 'em.

24:10.699 --> 24:11.700
[Jinman] Wouldn't that work?

24:11.784 --> 24:12.785
Find out quickly.

24:14.578 --> 24:17.414
Right, but I think I got a hold
of some info that you're gonna wanna hear.

24:18.207 --> 24:19.875
Yeah. You should know.

24:19.959 --> 24:21.877
-[Jinman] Yeah?
-What?

24:21.961 --> 24:24.880
I'm guessing you don't know what's in
that casket, do you?

24:24.964 --> 24:26.006
[Jinman] Well?

24:29.093 --> 24:31.553
You don't know, huh?
Well, I do.

24:32.763 --> 24:34.515
[inhales sharply]

24:36.225 --> 24:37.768
What's in it?

24:37.851 --> 24:40.938
Well, this info's worth
at least 100 gold chips.

24:41.021 --> 24:42.606
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
We can do that.

24:44.817 --> 24:46.652
Gold bars.

24:48.654 --> 24:50.280
[Jinman] A ton of them.

24:51.115 --> 24:52.449
[Jinman] One ton.

24:53.367 --> 24:54.618
The current market value...

24:56.245 --> 24:57.621
150 billion.

24:57.705 --> 24:59.498
[Jinman] Crazy, right?

25:00.582 --> 25:03.377
[Jinman] But then again,
you know what's really crazy?

25:03.460 --> 25:09.299
Is that, well, the chairman didn't
tell you you'd be smuggling gold, huh?

25:09.383 --> 25:10.801
Why is that?

25:11.552 --> 25:13.929
Seems like the kind of important stuff
you should know.

25:16.306 --> 25:18.892
[Jinman] I mean,
you are his right-hand man.

25:18.976 --> 25:20.686
[Jinman] Does that mean...

25:20.769 --> 25:22.604
...is he demoting you?

25:24.356 --> 25:26.400
[Jinman] Guess it doesn't matter.

25:27.151 --> 25:28.610
[Jinman] As long as you get the job done.
STYLE
::cue()

25:34.283 --> 25:36.410
Yeah. So.

25:36.493 --> 25:39.038
I heard that you're one
of the best goldsmiths in the area.

25:40.080 --> 25:43.167
Uh, yes, well...

25:43.250 --> 25:45.627
-You've manufactured gold bars yourself?
-[Hoonseok] Yes.

25:45.711 --> 25:48.047
[Woogy] I need you to make ten bars.

25:48.130 --> 25:50.299
One kilo each, just like
I said on the phone.

25:50.382 --> 25:52.051
And of course we'll provide the gold.

25:53.093 --> 25:54.219
[Woogy] And your casting fee?

25:54.303 --> 25:55.429
Mm...

25:57.598 --> 25:58.807
One percent of cost.

25:58.891 --> 26:00.893
[Woogy] Pretty good, right?

26:00.976 --> 26:03.145
It's not every day you get
an offer like this.

26:04.396 --> 26:06.857
[Woogy] I'm curious,
how long will it take to make them?

26:07.816 --> 26:09.443
Around two to three days.

26:09.526 --> 26:11.236
-Two to three.
-[Hoonseok] You see,

26:11.320 --> 26:12.196
gold bars don't require...

26:12.279 --> 26:13.739
[shushes]

26:14.948 --> 26:16.658
Detailed craftsmanship.

26:17.242 --> 26:18.243
One thing, though.

26:18.327 --> 26:20.788
Where in Jeongsan are you from, exactly?

26:21.705 --> 26:23.707
[Hoonseok] Don't you have a business card?

26:23.791 --> 26:25.584
It's just that normally gold bars

26:25.667 --> 26:28.462
are manufactured
in specific authorized factories,

26:28.545 --> 26:29.755
so why don't you go to those?

26:29.838 --> 26:31.298
The thing is...

26:32.800 --> 26:34.843
There's a reason why I'm paying you such
a high fee.

26:36.220 --> 26:37.554
It comes with one condition.

26:38.597 --> 26:39.807
What condition, you ask?

26:39.890 --> 26:41.308
No questions.

26:41.391 --> 26:44.686
[Woogy] The who, what, why, where,
none of it.

26:44.770 --> 26:46.814
They say silence is golden, right?

26:46.897 --> 26:50.818
[Woogy] So stay silent
and you can call it a golden fee.

26:50.901 --> 26:52.528
A golden fee?

26:52.611 --> 26:53.862
[Woogy] Yeah, that's right.

26:53.946 --> 26:55.697
And there's a second condition.

26:55.781 --> 26:57.074
It's not just questions.

26:57.157 --> 26:58.659
You can't say anything.

26:58.742 --> 26:59.743
[Woogy] You can't go around saying,

26:59.827 --> 27:02.496
"Hey, I'm working on this gold job.
They're 10-kilo bars,"

27:02.579 --> 27:04.456
to literally anyone.
If you do,

27:04.540 --> 27:06.041
our contract is over.

27:06.125 --> 27:08.836
[Woogy] Not only that,
your life will be over.

27:08.919 --> 27:10.254
Then you bought them illegally.

27:11.255 --> 27:12.548
[Hoonseok] If I refuse now...

27:13.465 --> 27:14.925
...I'll be okay, right?

27:18.095 --> 27:19.388
Of course.

27:19.471 --> 27:23.392
Mm, it's not like you saw
the gold or anything.

27:23.475 --> 27:25.060
So yeah,
if you don't wanna do it,

27:25.143 --> 27:27.271
no biggie.
It's not like anyone saw us here.

27:27.354 --> 27:31.775
No one knows that we met to talk and-
two percent, okay?

27:33.277 --> 27:34.486
3K per kilo.

27:35.362 --> 27:37.447
300 million for ten bars.

27:37.531 --> 27:39.032
[Woogy] Do you know anyone
who makes that in a month?

27:39.950 --> 27:42.244
I wouldn't offer this to anybody else,
Hoonseok.

27:42.327 --> 27:44.204
I like your face.

27:44.288 --> 27:47.457
[Woogy] You look like the type of guy
who'd make gold bars with total precision.

27:47.541 --> 27:49.126
I really want to work with you, okay?

27:51.211 --> 27:52.796
But if you'd rather refuse, say so, hmm?

27:52.880 --> 27:54.840
I'm a busy man.
I have to go look for someone else now.

27:54.923 --> 27:57.593
-We're done here.
-[Hoonseok] The gold bar.

27:58.635 --> 28:01.096
Show me.
Then I'll decide.

28:03.348 --> 28:04.349
Okay.

28:09.938 --> 28:12.566
Here. This is it.

28:12.649 --> 28:13.775
[Hoonseok] Okay.

28:21.241 --> 28:22.826
[Woogy sniffs]
Here he is.

28:22.910 --> 28:24.286
Mr. Lee Hoonseok.

28:25.787 --> 28:27.039
Yeah.

28:27.122 --> 28:28.916
And this is, uh...

28:30.042 --> 28:31.126
Call her Boss.

28:32.544 --> 28:34.963
Nice to meet you, Boss.

28:36.089 --> 28:37.466
Hello.

28:37.883 --> 28:39.134
[Woogy] He's going to work with us.

28:39.217 --> 28:40.552
He'll make the...

28:42.554 --> 28:44.306
You know what?
I've noticed your voice is kind of loud,

28:44.389 --> 28:46.475
so from now on we'll call
the gold bars "potatoes," okay?

28:47.225 --> 28:48.310
Show him the potato.

28:49.561 --> 28:51.229
[Woogy] He wants to check it.
STYLE
::cue()

28:54.775 --> 28:56.318
Hey, it's okay.
You're good to show him.

28:58.028 --> 28:59.655
[Woogy] We're all in the same boat now
so it's cool.

29:01.031 --> 29:02.950
[bag rustling and unzipping]

29:04.618 --> 29:06.244
[Heeju grunts]

29:06.328 --> 29:09.623
[both grunting]

29:09.706 --> 29:11.249
Here.

29:11.333 --> 29:12.876
[Woogy grunts]

29:12.960 --> 29:14.044
[exhales sharply]

29:17.506 --> 29:20.092
[scraping]

29:32.729 --> 29:34.523
This is real.

29:35.899 --> 29:37.901
Well, of course it is.
It's the real deal.

29:40.153 --> 29:41.655
All right, I'll have it done.

29:41.738 --> 29:43.448
It won't take long.
Come back tomorrow night.

29:43.532 --> 29:45.033
Uh, no, no, no.

29:46.493 --> 29:47.494
It'd be better...

29:47.577 --> 29:49.579
[grunts]

29:49.663 --> 29:50.831
[Heeju] ...if you could start work today.

29:50.914 --> 29:52.416
-[Heeju] And I would like to supervise.
-[grunts]

29:52.499 --> 29:55.293
That's right. And while she's watching,
I'll also be watching.

29:56.837 --> 29:58.380
I can't do it right away.

29:58.463 --> 30:01.216
I need to get things like
a new crucible and new molds,

30:01.299 --> 30:02.718
and if we're stamping
the Korea Mint mark...

30:02.801 --> 30:03.844
I can wait.

30:04.761 --> 30:06.471
[Woogy] Yeah, yeah.
We can wait.

30:06.555 --> 30:09.016
Hey, you can understand
why she's suspicious.

30:09.099 --> 30:10.976
You can get all those things today, right?

30:11.059 --> 30:13.103
Then we can get started tonight, huh?

30:13.186 --> 30:14.312
Pull an all-nighter?

30:16.648 --> 30:17.983
How about this?

30:19.234 --> 30:20.360
Midnight tonight.

30:21.278 --> 30:22.863
Come to the front of the workshop.

30:24.823 --> 30:26.283
When everything's all set,
I'll give you guys a call.

30:26.366 --> 30:27.743
-And I'll let you inside.
-[Woogy] Nice.

30:27.826 --> 30:29.036
[Heeju] All right.

30:29.119 --> 30:30.120
So I'll call you later.

30:31.913 --> 30:33.623
-See you at midnight.
-Mm-hmm.

30:33.707 --> 30:35.667
Call us. Call us later.

30:36.376 --> 30:37.377
[car door closes]

30:38.962 --> 30:40.505
[exhales sharply]

30:41.673 --> 30:42.883
[Woogy] See?

30:42.966 --> 30:44.301
What'd I say?

30:44.384 --> 30:46.011
There's nothing money can't buy.

30:46.094 --> 30:49.181
Do you really think he's the right guy?

30:49.264 --> 30:50.599
He seems too nice.

30:51.892 --> 30:53.143
So? What's wrong with being a nice guy?

30:53.226 --> 30:54.478
[Heeju] He could have a sudden change
of heart

30:54.561 --> 30:57.522
and decide to report us to the police.

30:57.606 --> 30:59.066
Stop worrying about that.

30:59.149 --> 31:01.026
I told you I did
a background check on the guy.

31:01.943 --> 31:03.278
That guy there?

31:04.196 --> 31:06.198
He lives with his widowed mother
and sister.

31:06.281 --> 31:08.158
He's the breadwinner of the family.

31:08.241 --> 31:09.493
So what?

31:10.619 --> 31:11.953
[exhales sharply]
Heeju.

31:12.788 --> 31:15.123
This is how we make deals in my world,
okay?

31:15.207 --> 31:17.125
Money's important
but collateral's necessary.

31:17.209 --> 31:18.502
It's absolutely essential.

31:18.585 --> 31:21.046
Last thing you want
is to get stabbed in the back.

31:21.129 --> 31:23.381
So you always have to consider
the worst-case scenario.

31:23.465 --> 31:24.883
And these guys?

31:24.966 --> 31:27.928
What's the one thing that keeps them
from doing something stupid or crazy?

31:28.011 --> 31:29.763
Collateral, of course.

31:29.846 --> 31:31.389
The more important the collateral is,

31:31.473 --> 31:33.183
the less likely they are
to screw us over.

31:34.643 --> 31:35.894
So you're saying...

31:37.062 --> 31:40.398
...his mom and younger sister
are collateral?

31:43.110 --> 31:45.821
-Ah, come on. You know what I mean.
-[Heeju] Then what's my collateral?

31:45.904 --> 31:47.364
Is it my aunt?

31:49.449 --> 31:50.450
Heeju.

31:50.534 --> 31:51.910
That's why you went to the pawn shop
the other day.

31:51.993 --> 31:53.370
To check on my collateral?

31:53.453 --> 31:55.122
Are you seriously asking me that?

31:55.205 --> 31:56.790
I went because I wanted to see Auntie.

31:56.873 --> 31:59.584
You got it all wrong.
It's not like that.

31:59.668 --> 32:00.961
Ah, come on.

32:01.044 --> 32:02.337
Collateral's insane.

32:02.420 --> 32:04.464
How 'bout we go eat?
What do you want?

32:04.548 --> 32:05.924
[grunts]

32:06.007 --> 32:07.259
Bokjiri sounds good..
STYLE
::cue()

32:09.928 --> 32:13.014
[crickets chirping]

32:13.098 --> 32:14.349
[Heeju] Something's wrong.

32:15.642 --> 32:16.810
Give him a call.

32:16.893 --> 32:18.186
[Woogy] Well, he said he'd call
when he's ready.

32:18.270 --> 32:19.563
[cell phone vibrates]

32:23.316 --> 32:24.317
Yeah?

32:25.694 --> 32:26.736
Mm, okay.

32:28.864 --> 32:30.115
[Woogy grunting]

32:31.283 --> 32:34.119
[breathing heavily]

32:59.895 --> 33:02.480
JEIL WORKSHOP

33:02.564 --> 33:04.065
[keypad beeping]

33:05.525 --> 33:06.776
[door locks unlocking]

33:06.860 --> 33:08.111
[door squeaks]

33:08.195 --> 33:09.404
[light switches click]

33:09.487 --> 33:12.199
[whirring]

33:17.704 --> 33:19.831
[door locks beeping]

33:21.875 --> 33:23.210
Oh, here.

33:23.293 --> 33:24.419
Oh.

33:32.928 --> 33:34.763
[Woogy] I got it.

33:34.846 --> 33:36.014
Here.

33:36.097 --> 33:37.974
[both grunting]

33:38.058 --> 33:39.142
[gold bar thuds]

33:39.226 --> 33:41.186
[zipper unzips]

33:43.271 --> 33:44.814
How long will it take?

33:44.898 --> 33:47.400
I'll be done with it before morning.

33:47.484 --> 33:50.278
I guess you two just wait here.

33:52.113 --> 33:55.116
Yeah, and don't you even think
about pulling any stunts.

33:55.200 --> 33:56.993
I'll be watching you.

33:58.119 --> 33:59.871
[Woogy] I'm watching you over there, too!

33:59.955 --> 34:03.375
[scraping]

34:05.877 --> 34:07.337
[exhales sharply]

34:07.420 --> 34:08.797
[heat hissing]

34:08.880 --> 34:10.340
[exhales]

34:11.967 --> 34:13.802
[bar clinking]

34:16.012 --> 34:16.972
[hissing]

34:17.055 --> 34:18.139
[door clangs]

34:23.645 --> 34:25.438
[fire roars]

34:30.610 --> 34:33.613
[flames hissing]

34:43.665 --> 34:46.668
[melted gold splatting]

34:50.130 --> 34:53.174
[flames hiss]

34:54.259 --> 34:55.844
[gold clinks]

34:56.928 --> 34:58.805
[water sizzling]

35:03.143 --> 35:04.811
[bars clink]

35:04.894 --> 35:07.856
[flames roaring]

35:07.939 --> 35:09.941
[cell phone vibrating]

35:10.025 --> 35:13.570
INCOMING CALL
JEIL WORKSHOP PRESIDENT NOH

35:13.653 --> 35:16.656
JEWELRY ECONOMY DAILY

35:16.740 --> 35:19.367
[distant gold clinking]

35:19.451 --> 35:20.577
[exhales]

35:21.328 --> 35:22.454
That's right.

35:27.626 --> 35:29.753
You went into that coal mine.

35:30.670 --> 35:32.839
[distant thunder rumbling]

35:32.922 --> 35:34.382
[thunder cracks]

35:34.466 --> 35:35.925
DAD! BE SAFE AGAIN TODAY

35:48.813 --> 35:50.023
You were there?

35:50.982 --> 35:53.652
Of course I was.

35:55.528 --> 35:56.946
[exhales]

35:57.030 --> 35:59.324
[inhales and exhales sharply]

36:00.408 --> 36:01.534
What was the name of that mutt, again?

36:02.994 --> 36:04.746
[Woogy] Mongsil or something.

36:05.955 --> 36:07.248
Don't you remember?

36:07.332 --> 36:09.125
You went in there while we
were playing freeze tag, I think.

36:11.211 --> 36:12.837
[Woogy] You were looking
for that stupid dog

36:12.921 --> 36:14.589
and I waited for you forever.

36:14.673 --> 36:15.965
[newspaper page turns]

36:16.049 --> 36:18.343
I kept waiting,
but you didn't come out.

36:18.426 --> 36:20.762
So I went to get the Aunties.

36:23.014 --> 36:25.016
[9-Year-Old Heeju] Mongsil, wait!
STYLE
::cue()

36:25.100 --> 36:26.893
[dog yaps]

36:26.976 --> 36:28.436
[9-Year-Old Heeju] Mongsil!

36:29.854 --> 36:30.939
[distant dog yaps]

36:32.941 --> 36:34.192
Mongsil!

36:37.028 --> 36:38.863
Mongsil, here!

36:48.206 --> 36:49.541
[9-Year-Old Heeju] Mongsil!

36:52.669 --> 36:53.878
Heeju.

36:56.214 --> 36:57.298
[Woogy] You don't remember?

36:58.216 --> 36:59.426
[exhales]

37:00.468 --> 37:03.471
I'm not sure.
I don't think so.

37:05.557 --> 37:07.267
You really forgot.

37:08.351 --> 37:10.603
[Woogy] Come on.
You gotta remember.

37:10.687 --> 37:12.897
I practically saved your life, you know?

37:13.773 --> 37:14.774
[Heeju] I don't know.

37:14.858 --> 37:16.359
[Heeju] I seriously don't remember.

37:17.861 --> 37:19.279
[Woogy exhales sharply]

37:21.030 --> 37:22.031
[sighs]

37:23.324 --> 37:26.828
[cell phone vibrating]

37:43.386 --> 37:45.930
[door lock beeping]

37:46.973 --> 37:48.892
[chiming]

37:48.975 --> 37:50.393
[door handle rattles]

37:50.477 --> 37:52.228
Hoonseok?

37:52.312 --> 37:54.105
[gasps and shushes]

37:54.189 --> 37:56.524
-[Hoonseok] Shh, quiet. Quiet.
-[President Noh] Are you there?

37:57.358 --> 37:58.359
Who is it?

37:59.736 --> 38:01.154
[Woogy] Hey! What are you doing?

38:01.237 --> 38:03.740
It's-it's the owner.

38:03.823 --> 38:05.450
[all gasping]

38:05.533 --> 38:06.701
Hold on.

38:08.328 --> 38:09.788
[gold clinking]

38:09.871 --> 38:11.206
Hoonseok!

38:13.082 --> 38:14.292
Quick, come on.

38:14.375 --> 38:15.794
-Come on.
-[President Noh] Are you asleep?

38:15.877 --> 38:17.086
[gasps]

38:20.507 --> 38:22.133
[President Noh] Hoonseok.

38:22.217 --> 38:24.344
[locks clacking]

38:25.470 --> 38:26.763
Ah, goodness.

38:26.846 --> 38:28.973
So you were in here.

38:29.057 --> 38:30.391
Yes. What are you...

38:30.475 --> 38:32.519
Well, why did you lock the door?

38:32.602 --> 38:34.479
What are you doing up at this hour?

38:36.940 --> 38:38.608
Uh, sir, can I talk to you for a sec?

38:40.610 --> 38:41.611
Hold on.

38:44.113 --> 38:47.033
[Hoonseok] There's nothing...

38:48.618 --> 38:49.661
[Hoonseok] Sir?

38:51.996 --> 38:53.665
Wait.

38:53.748 --> 38:55.750
What-what's all that?

38:58.795 --> 39:00.964
-[nervous exhale]
-[President Noh] Spit it out!

39:01.047 --> 39:02.340
[President Noh] What are you up to?

39:03.341 --> 39:05.802
[Hoonseok] Someone from Janggak asked me
to do some craft work.

39:05.885 --> 39:07.262
Let go.

39:07.345 --> 39:08.346
[both grunting]

39:08.429 --> 39:10.682
[President Noh] What? Seems like a lot.

39:10.765 --> 39:13.601
[Hoonseok] It's 14k.
There's not much gold in it.

39:14.978 --> 39:16.145
[Hoonseok] Hold on, sir!

39:16.229 --> 39:17.105
Why do you wanna go in there?

39:17.188 --> 39:19.399
[Hoonseok] There's nothing to...

39:19.482 --> 39:20.817
Goodness, what's with you?

39:20.900 --> 39:22.235
[President Noh grunts]

39:26.364 --> 39:27.907
What are you doing at this hour?

39:27.991 --> 39:29.200
Why aren't you at home sleeping?

39:32.871 --> 39:34.205
[President Noh groans]

39:34.289 --> 39:35.707
I couldn't sleep.

39:35.790 --> 39:37.292
[exhales sharply]

39:39.043 --> 39:41.838
I decided to sell this factory
to President Choi.

39:42.797 --> 39:44.215
[President Noh]
It's best you stop working here...

39:45.967 --> 39:47.343
...and look somewhere else.

39:47.427 --> 39:48.595
But sir...

39:49.596 --> 39:51.055
I'm very sorry.

39:51.764 --> 39:53.641
I wanted to help you send your sister
to college.

39:54.559 --> 39:56.644
And of course I wanted to help your mom.

39:56.728 --> 39:59.439
Make sure you could take care
of her while she's unwell.

40:00.148 --> 40:02.817
[President Noh] But there's just
no way I can hold on anymore.

40:04.819 --> 40:06.446
Forget about me.

40:06.529 --> 40:09.157
What are you going
to do about paying off your loan?

40:09.240 --> 40:12.243
I thought you said Mr. Choi's offer
wasn't that great.

40:12.327 --> 40:14.954
[chuckles]
Look, I wasn't good enough.

40:15.038 --> 40:17.081
[President Noh] That's why I'm in debt.
What can you do?

40:17.165 --> 40:18.875
[President Noh exhales sharply]
Okay.

40:20.376 --> 40:21.544
Be careful.

40:21.628 --> 40:24.547
I hear there are a lot
of thieves stealing gold dust.

40:25.256 --> 40:27.008
Better keep the doors locked up.

40:27.091 --> 40:28.343
Yeah.

40:28.426 --> 40:30.261
Thank you.

40:30.345 --> 40:32.722
You've always been a hard worker.

40:32.805 --> 40:33.806
[chuckles]

40:33.890 --> 40:35.058
[exhales]

40:37.352 --> 40:38.353
[relieved exhale]
STYLE
::cue()

40:42.857 --> 40:44.901
[gold bar clatters]
[both gasp]

40:44.984 --> 40:45.985
[clanging]

40:47.445 --> 40:49.113
Wait a minute.
What was that noise?

40:49.989 --> 40:52.283
Uh, what noise?
I didn't hear any noise.

40:52.367 --> 40:54.285
-What's wrong with you?
-[Hoonseok] Nothing.

40:54.369 --> 40:55.370
Get out of my way, kid!

40:55.453 --> 40:57.580
-[President Noh] What was that?
-[Hoonseok] That was nothing!

40:57.664 --> 40:59.958
-[Hoonseok] You should just go...
-I'm going in!

41:00.041 --> 41:02.377
Sir, wait, please!
Don't go in there!

41:03.753 --> 41:04.796
[all shouting]

41:05.755 --> 41:09.467
[blow lands]
[all yelling]

41:09.550 --> 41:11.302
We're fucked.
We're so fucked.

41:11.386 --> 41:12.553
Sir, are you okay?

41:14.013 --> 41:16.099
Why'd you do that?

41:16.182 --> 41:18.685
Sir, are you okay?

41:20.019 --> 41:21.604
[Heeju] He needs to go to the hospital.

41:23.564 --> 41:25.400
[Heeju] We have to take him, okay?

41:27.235 --> 41:29.278
[Heeju] Woogy. Hey. Hey!

41:29.362 --> 41:30.613
What are you doing?

41:31.447 --> 41:32.448
We have no choice.

41:32.532 --> 41:33.992
He saw the gold bar
so I gotta finish him off.

41:34.075 --> 41:35.034
-No!
-[Hoonseok] Are you crazy?

41:35.118 --> 41:36.869
-[both grunting]
-Let go.

41:36.953 --> 41:38.037
Let go!

41:38.121 --> 41:40.206
[Heeju] Wait! Wait a second!

41:40.289 --> 41:42.041
Just-just put that down, okay?

41:42.125 --> 41:43.751
If you don't wanna help,
get out of the way.

41:44.669 --> 41:46.462
-[Woogy] I gotta cut him into pieces.
-No! You can't do that, no!

41:46.546 --> 41:47.755
[Heeju] Cut him up?

41:47.839 --> 41:49.632
-He's alive still!
-[Woogy] Is he?

41:49.716 --> 41:51.509
I guess I just have to kill him, then!

41:51.592 --> 41:52.635
You want the gold?

41:52.719 --> 41:54.053
[Woogy] Then fucking move!

41:54.137 --> 41:55.722
-No, you can't! You can't!
-[Woogy] Get off!

41:55.805 --> 41:57.682
[Hoonseok] I can talk to him!

41:57.765 --> 41:59.392
I can say you were thieves!
He won't know about the gold!

41:59.475 --> 42:01.686
[Heeju] Yeah! L-let him take him
to the hospital.

42:01.769 --> 42:03.646
After that, we can let
Hoonseok take care of it.

42:03.730 --> 42:05.231
Enough. Move out of the way.

42:05.314 --> 42:07.025
[all shouting]

42:07.108 --> 42:10.111
If you kill my boss,
then you'll have to kill me, too!

42:10.194 --> 42:11.487
Or else I'll spill everything I know!

42:11.571 --> 42:13.364
[Heeju] If you do this,

42:13.448 --> 42:16.159
then you and I are through!
You gonna kill me as well?

42:16.242 --> 42:18.745
[all breathing heavily]

42:18.828 --> 42:21.831
[Heeju] Woogy. Woogy, please.

42:23.249 --> 42:24.709
You always used to listen to me.

42:24.792 --> 42:26.669
[Heeju] When we were kids.

42:28.671 --> 42:29.672
[Heeju] At the coal mine.

42:29.756 --> 42:31.382
And I fell down.

42:32.175 --> 42:34.385
It was you who saved me, right?

42:35.636 --> 42:37.055
[both breathing heavily]

42:37.138 --> 42:38.681
That's right.

42:39.599 --> 42:41.350
I remember.

42:41.434 --> 42:42.477
It's just...

42:44.353 --> 42:45.688
...I didn't wanna remember it.

42:53.654 --> 42:54.947
Fuck.

42:55.031 --> 42:56.324
[tool clanging]

42:56.407 --> 42:59.452
[relieved heavy breaths]

43:11.339 --> 43:13.800
-Whoa, no!
-[Woogy] Hey! What?

43:13.883 --> 43:15.009
We're taking him to the hospital, right?

43:15.843 --> 43:19.639
[Hoonseok] Wait, wait, wait!
Behind your back, you-you have a knife.

43:20.723 --> 43:22.725
[Woogy exhales sharply]
Fuck.

43:27.897 --> 43:30.900
[strained breathing]

43:31.943 --> 43:35.321
Ah, fuck these damn
conscientious assholes.

43:35.404 --> 43:37.949
[labored breathing]

43:38.032 --> 43:39.492
[Woogy] Oh, what the fuck am I doing?

43:40.159 --> 43:42.120
[Woogy breathing heavily]

43:42.954 --> 43:44.163
[Woogy] Is this even right?

43:44.789 --> 43:48.626
[Woogy] Ah, what is this shit? Ah!

43:48.709 --> 43:51.254
[electricity buzzing]

43:51.337 --> 43:54.340
[machines rumbling]

43:56.551 --> 43:57.593
[metal clangs]

43:58.594 --> 44:01.973
[hammer clinking]

44:22.660 --> 44:24.453
[gold bars clinking]
STYLE
::cue()

44:27.874 --> 44:31.961
[clinking]

44:42.013 --> 44:43.806
[Hoonseok] Okay.

44:43.890 --> 44:46.726
If they're off by point-one gram,
there's no need to worry.

44:46.809 --> 44:51.022
That's within the normal weight range,
so you'll sell them without any issues.

44:51.105 --> 44:54.233
As for the leftover dust and fragments,
I'll keep them here,

44:54.317 --> 44:56.444
and I'll mix them in when I do
the next casting.

44:56.527 --> 44:57.695
[Heeju exhales]

44:57.778 --> 44:59.488
Thank you so much.
You did good work.

45:00.573 --> 45:01.991
Nice work.

45:02.074 --> 45:03.784
I'll be back in three days, 'kay?

45:03.868 --> 45:05.286
And the cash?

45:06.078 --> 45:07.205
[Woogy] Didn't we tell you?

45:08.664 --> 45:09.665
You didn't tell him?

45:09.749 --> 45:11.209
What?

45:12.251 --> 45:13.961
Well, it's a deferred payment.

45:14.045 --> 45:15.671
[Woogy] I'll settle it in three days.

45:15.755 --> 45:17.173
[Hoonseok] Wait, wait, wait.
Wait a minute.

45:17.256 --> 45:18.382
Uh, deferred?

45:18.466 --> 45:20.301
Come on.

45:21.219 --> 45:22.386
Shit, you don't trust us?

45:22.470 --> 45:24.347
Of course I don't trust you!

45:24.430 --> 45:27.475
How do I know you two will actually
come back in three days?

45:27.558 --> 45:29.101
Well, what do you want?

45:29.185 --> 45:30.436
[Woogy] I don't have it!
I don't have the cash!

45:30.519 --> 45:33.731
Hold on. We-we agreed
to give you two percent, didn't we?

45:33.814 --> 45:34.982
Yeah.

45:36.692 --> 45:37.693
[Heeju] Well, this...

45:37.777 --> 45:39.070
[grunts]

45:39.153 --> 45:41.239
...is worth 150 mil.

45:41.322 --> 45:43.241
[Heeju] Consider this half upfront.

45:43.324 --> 45:46.077
And you'll get the rest once
the job is done.

45:46.994 --> 45:47.995
Oh.

45:49.956 --> 45:53.167
Wow. You really scored.

45:53.918 --> 45:55.211
Lucky you.

45:55.920 --> 45:58.047
Give it to me.
I'll exchange it for you.

45:58.130 --> 46:01.175
No, thanks.
I can take care of it myself.

46:02.385 --> 46:05.846
And you'll promise us that you'll be able
to work on the rest, too?

46:07.098 --> 46:09.725
Yes, Boss.
I'll do it because I trust you.

46:09.809 --> 46:10.810
[relieved exhale]

46:11.727 --> 46:13.938
But I don't trust him at all.

46:14.021 --> 46:17.733
You motherfucker. You think you can point
your finger and say that shit to my face?

46:17.817 --> 46:19.277
[Woogy] Who the fuck do you think you are?

46:19.360 --> 46:20.444
-You wanna die?
-See you next time.

46:20.528 --> 46:22.280
What a piece of shit.
Hey, hey!

46:22.363 --> 46:24.156
[Woogy] I don't trust you either, you
prick!

46:24.240 --> 46:26.742
-[Woogy] Where's my knife? No!
-[Heeju] Stop it. Come on. Come on.

46:35.084 --> 46:36.085
Sorry.

46:37.211 --> 46:39.088
I got worked up earlier.

46:40.715 --> 46:43.050
The whole situation kinda got out
of control.

46:46.345 --> 46:47.596
Do you need a doctor?

46:48.472 --> 46:49.473
Forget it.

46:50.391 --> 46:52.435
Instead, I need your word.

46:53.269 --> 46:57.064
If you and I are going to work together,
you won't kill anyone.

46:57.148 --> 47:01.235
[Heeju] If you ever pull a knife
or spill blood one more time,

47:01.319 --> 47:03.112
you and I are done.
It's over.

47:04.322 --> 47:05.323
[Woogy scoffs]

47:07.366 --> 47:09.368
What if someone finds out
we're doing this?

47:13.247 --> 47:14.248
[inhales and exhales sharply]

47:14.332 --> 47:16.792
You think you're being
fucking conscientious?

47:16.876 --> 47:17.877
Hmm?

47:20.421 --> 47:22.256
That mindset doesn't make
any fucking sense

47:22.340 --> 47:23.466
for a wannabe thief.

47:24.383 --> 47:27.928
[Woogy] Fuck.
You're stealing gold, you know.

47:28.012 --> 47:30.556
A whopping 100 kilograms
of someone else's gold.

47:31.265 --> 47:34.477
And now you want the money?
All in good conscience?

47:34.560 --> 47:36.395
[Woogy] Without getting blood
on your hands?

47:37.772 --> 47:39.231
[exhales sharply]

47:41.901 --> 47:43.611
Well, then.

47:43.694 --> 47:45.404
Do you promise or not?

47:47.365 --> 47:48.657
[exhales sharply]

47:48.741 --> 47:50.242
Yeah, I'll do my best.

47:50.326 --> 47:53.329
[♪ dramatic music]

47:59.168 --> 48:00.169
[Woogy] Here.
STYLE
::cue()

48:13.808 --> 48:14.892
[exhales]

48:17.937 --> 48:20.940
[distant birds chirping]

48:21.023 --> 48:24.026
[♪ dramatic music continues]

48:40.209 --> 48:41.836
[door creaks open]

48:50.344 --> 48:51.345
[Heeju gasps]

48:51.429 --> 48:52.805
[shuddering]

48:52.888 --> 48:54.515
[Sunok] How much longer
are you gonna sleep?

48:54.598 --> 48:56.434
It's already dark out.

48:57.476 --> 48:58.894
Keep still.

49:00.312 --> 49:01.313
[Sunok] Almost done.

49:15.911 --> 49:16.912
Go.

49:18.664 --> 49:20.040
Get out of here.

49:22.084 --> 49:23.335
[Sunok] Run away.

49:23.419 --> 49:25.254
I'll pay off all of your debt for you.

49:26.172 --> 49:28.757
Do you even have the money
to pay off my debt?

49:29.383 --> 49:30.593
You don't even know what I owe.

49:31.677 --> 49:33.137
How much is it?

49:33.220 --> 49:34.513
[exhales sharply]

49:36.182 --> 49:37.475
I don't have debt.

49:38.934 --> 49:41.020
When it's time, I'll leave quietly.
Don't worry.

49:42.021 --> 49:43.063
Where were you last night?

49:45.191 --> 49:46.817
Were you hanging out with that thug?

49:48.110 --> 49:50.154
-What on Earth did you do with your hand?
-I already told you,

49:50.237 --> 49:51.614
there's nothing going on!

49:52.990 --> 49:54.074
And my hand...

49:55.284 --> 49:56.744
I just fell, okay?

49:56.827 --> 49:58.787
Don't tell me it was from a fall!
It was from a knife.

49:58.871 --> 50:00.206
Enough, all right.

50:01.123 --> 50:03.667
Wow. You luckless bitch.

50:03.751 --> 50:04.793
[surprised exhale]

50:04.877 --> 50:06.962
You ran away and still ended up like this.

50:09.089 --> 50:10.132
[both exhale]

50:11.550 --> 50:13.594
You wanna know what's really ridiculous?

50:14.637 --> 50:18.516
Everyone can tell that the bitch
with the worst luck is you.

50:19.892 --> 50:22.603
So hearing you call me that
just makes me furious.

50:23.646 --> 50:25.231
It really pisses me off.

50:28.526 --> 50:30.528
Don't put all your trust
into men like that.

50:32.154 --> 50:34.073
One moment can ruin your whole life.

50:34.156 --> 50:35.574
You're one to talk.

50:35.658 --> 50:37.910
Then why did you marry that trash?

50:37.993 --> 50:39.620
[Sunok] To survive.

50:39.703 --> 50:42.122
You think I could pay off my debt
and raise a kid by serving coffee?

50:42.206 --> 50:44.416
-If it weren't for you I would've...
-[Heeju] Don't use me as an excuse!

50:44.500 --> 50:46.252
I never asked for any of that!

50:47.711 --> 50:49.964
Every single moment I had to spend
with that man was nothing but hell!

50:50.047 --> 50:51.131
An do you think I was happy?

50:51.215 --> 50:53.884
That's why I begged you to run away!

50:53.968 --> 50:55.219
[Heeju] You didn't wanna go, though!

50:55.302 --> 50:57.471
[Heeju] Even after I told you what
that man tried to do to me, you...

50:57.555 --> 50:59.723
[Sunok] What is the point
of dredging this up now?

50:59.807 --> 51:01.350
Should I beg for your forgiveness?

51:01.433 --> 51:02.977
-Would that make it better?
-[Heeju] Yes!

51:03.894 --> 51:05.396
Beg and apologize.

51:05.479 --> 51:07.064
So I can feel better.

51:07.147 --> 51:08.649
[labored breathing]

51:13.737 --> 51:16.907
[door opens and closes]

51:16.991 --> 51:19.910
[whimpering]

51:19.994 --> 51:22.997
[crying]

51:30.504 --> 51:33.507
[pills rattling]

51:47.146 --> 51:50.149
[panicked breathing]

51:51.567 --> 51:53.110
[Sunok] Heeju, Heeju.
Don't come out.

51:53.193 --> 51:54.612
[Sunok] Your uncle is here.
[door closes]

51:59.700 --> 52:02.578
[door opens]

52:05.205 --> 52:07.291
Well? You glad to see me?

52:07.374 --> 52:08.792
It's been two months.

52:08.876 --> 52:12.254
Uh, I was about to close up here.

52:13.547 --> 52:15.841
[Sunok] Let's go home.
Did you eat?

52:21.764 --> 52:23.015
[Cheoljung] Get in here already.

52:26.226 --> 52:29.313
Hi. It's me again.
[chuckles]

52:29.396 --> 52:31.482
[door creaks]
STYLE
::cue()

52:33.817 --> 52:37.738
[Cheoljung] So I heard you sold a watch
to Mr. Jang a week ago.

52:37.821 --> 52:39.615
For 30 million.

52:40.866 --> 52:42.868
[exhales]
How much did you pay for it?

52:43.786 --> 52:45.663
You were able to sell for a high price.

52:45.746 --> 52:47.289
And you didn't tell me.

52:47.373 --> 52:49.208
[Mr. Jang clears throat]

52:49.291 --> 52:54.046
I mean, I thought the price was, well,
a little too high.

52:54.129 --> 52:55.631
So I let Han know.

52:56.715 --> 52:58.050
All right, bring me the ledger.

52:59.176 --> 53:02.179
[Cheoljung] I said bring me the ledger.

53:02.262 --> 53:05.099
[♪ suspenseful music]

53:20.948 --> 53:22.324
[exhales]

53:22.408 --> 53:24.076
What else did you say you took?

53:24.868 --> 53:27.371
[Mr. Jang] That's all for this month.
Wait, actually,

53:27.454 --> 53:29.415
I bought a few rings, too.

53:29.498 --> 53:31.375
I think she priced those correctly.

53:31.458 --> 53:32.710
[Mr. Jang chuckles]

53:33.794 --> 53:35.462
You said you got diamonds.

53:35.546 --> 53:37.756
'Bout a month ago.

53:41.719 --> 53:42.928
[Cheoljung exhales]

53:43.011 --> 53:44.054
No diamonds.

53:45.097 --> 53:47.015
Not even one.

53:52.229 --> 53:54.648
Is there a separate ledger for Janggak?

53:59.111 --> 54:00.320
[book lands on desk]

54:02.823 --> 54:04.324
[cigarette sizzles]

54:05.033 --> 54:06.326
You can go home now.

54:07.536 --> 54:09.037
[groans]

54:09.121 --> 54:12.249
I hope I didn't say anything that
was unnecessary.

54:12.332 --> 54:14.418
No, you were right to.

54:14.501 --> 54:16.545
I'm the owner and the husband.

54:17.212 --> 54:19.047
-Best that I know everything.
-Right.

54:19.131 --> 54:21.216
[Cheoljung] All right, then.
Take care.

54:21.300 --> 54:22.551
[Cheoljung exhales]

54:23.469 --> 54:25.012
Uh, I'll see you.

54:25.095 --> 54:26.221
[Cheoljung] Goodbye.

54:27.014 --> 54:28.974
[door creaks]

54:29.057 --> 54:30.100
[locks click]

54:30.934 --> 54:33.103
[cigarette sizzles]

54:34.563 --> 54:35.731
[exhales]

54:39.401 --> 54:41.570
[Cheoljung] You must
have really lost your mind.

54:42.696 --> 54:45.032
[inhales on cigarette]

54:45.115 --> 54:48.327
You were just a coffee shop girl
with a little kid.

54:48.410 --> 54:50.329
I took you in and fed you,

54:50.412 --> 54:52.956
and you thank me
by taking my money on the sly?

54:53.040 --> 54:54.625
[inhales]

54:54.708 --> 54:56.293
[exhales]

54:57.252 --> 54:58.253
[stomps out cigarette]

55:02.758 --> 55:04.134
When did this start?

55:06.261 --> 55:08.055
How much have you skimmed now?

55:10.933 --> 55:12.726
-That's all.
-[Sunok] Oh.

55:13.852 --> 55:15.521
Really?

55:17.356 --> 55:20.567
[Cheoljung exhales sharply]
You thieving bitch.

55:21.318 --> 55:24.196
Look at you still lying through
your fucking teeth!

55:24.279 --> 55:25.280
[slams hand on table]

55:30.369 --> 55:31.411
[Cheoljung] Shit!

55:32.621 --> 55:34.957
-[panicked breathing]
-[grunting]

55:35.040 --> 55:36.041
Where do you think you're going?

55:36.124 --> 55:37.543
-[screaming]
-[Cheoljung] Come here!

55:37.626 --> 55:39.795
[both shouting]

55:39.878 --> 55:41.129
[filing cabinet bangs]

55:41.213 --> 55:44.675
[Sunok groaning]

55:45.592 --> 55:47.719
Better not say you fucking spent it all.

55:47.803 --> 55:51.098
If you did, I swear I'll
send you straight to Heaven.

55:52.391 --> 55:53.892
[gasping]

55:53.976 --> 55:54.977
I swear.

55:55.060 --> 55:57.187
[gagging]

55:57.271 --> 55:58.605
[Sunok struggling]

55:58.689 --> 56:00.315
Hah!

56:00.399 --> 56:03.652
[groaning]

56:04.236 --> 56:05.821
[gasps]

56:07.489 --> 56:08.657
You won't say?

56:08.740 --> 56:11.827
[Cheoljung] You know I won't hesitate
to cut you.

56:11.910 --> 56:13.912
I am gonna check the ledgers.

56:13.996 --> 56:16.999
So why don't you just spit it out,
fucking bitch?

56:21.253 --> 56:23.046
[blow lands]
[groans]

56:23.130 --> 56:24.673
-[Cheoljung groans]
-[Sunok gasps]

56:26.383 --> 56:29.928
No, Heeju!
No, don't do it.

56:30.012 --> 56:32.764
[Heeju whimpering]

56:32.848 --> 56:34.016
[Sunok gasps]

56:34.099 --> 56:36.935
[blood squelching]

56:37.019 --> 56:39.896
[both breathing heavily]

56:42.316 --> 56:45.152
[Sunok] Go.
Hurry, hurry, go.

56:45.235 --> 56:47.070
Look at me and get a hold of yourself!

56:47.154 --> 56:49.114
Just grab what you need and go.

56:49.197 --> 56:50.449
I'll take care of everything.
STYLE
::cue()

56:53.660 --> 56:57.205
[drawers clanging]

57:01.084 --> 57:04.087
[both breathing heavily]

57:13.180 --> 57:15.432
[Sunok] Take this.
It's the money I've earned over the years.

57:16.475 --> 57:17.809
I've been saving it for you.

57:19.978 --> 57:22.439
So take it and don't ever come back.

57:22.522 --> 57:26.360
[Sunok] No matter what happens to me,
don't try to look for me.

57:26.443 --> 57:27.444
Don't try to find out.

57:28.445 --> 57:29.821
You go somewhere far away.

57:30.864 --> 57:32.491
I want you to live a good life.

57:33.492 --> 57:34.493
No.

57:35.786 --> 57:37.746
You have to go.

57:37.829 --> 57:40.457
I'm really sorry.
Heeju.

57:40.540 --> 57:42.584
[Sunok] I'm sorry.

57:42.668 --> 57:45.212
I need you to listen.
Just listen to me this once.

57:45.295 --> 57:47.339
Go! You going will save my life.

57:47.422 --> 57:49.716
[Sunok] Go. Go!

57:49.800 --> 57:51.718
[Heeju] Auntie! Auntie!

57:51.802 --> 57:52.803
-[Sunok] Go!
-[Heeju] Auntie!

57:52.886 --> 57:54.888
[Heeju crying]

57:54.971 --> 57:58.392
I told you to go! Go!
Hurry up and get outta here!

58:00.268 --> 58:02.729
[Sunok] I said go away! Go!

58:02.813 --> 58:06.274
[both crying]

58:06.358 --> 58:09.986
[whimpering]

58:14.449 --> 58:17.077
[sniffling]

58:33.051 --> 58:36.221
[cell phone trilling]

58:36.304 --> 58:37.305
[receiver clicks]

58:37.389 --> 58:39.057
[gasps]

58:39.141 --> 58:40.142
Hello.

58:40.684 --> 58:43.729
I-I'm in Bukju.

58:45.439 --> 58:47.399
[Sunok] The Happy Pawnshop in Bukju.

58:48.734 --> 58:52.571
[Sunok] I think I killed a person.

59:00.203 --> 59:03.206
[crying]

59:19.347 --> 59:20.807
[distant sirens wailing]

59:20.891 --> 59:23.894
[sirens approaching]

59:26.313 --> 59:27.939
[tires squeaking]

59:32.152 --> 59:34.362
[more sirens approaching]

59:34.446 --> 59:35.906
[brakes squeaking]

59:35.989 --> 59:37.199
Auntie.

59:37.282 --> 59:39.534
[crying]

59:39.618 --> 59:40.744
Mom.

59:40.827 --> 59:43.830
[crying]

59:47.751 --> 59:50.629
[sirens wailing]

59:50.712 --> 59:53.715
[Heeju crying]

59:53.799 --> 59:56.802
[♪ dramatic music]

01:00:23.161 --> 01:00:26.164
[♪ dramatic music continues]
